The package BQPD (Roger Fletcher, U. Dundee) is not included 
as part of GALAHAD, but may be called optionally from GALAHAD's 
ubersolver QP package.

GALAHAD relies on a single environment variable,
and if BQPD is not available, this is set as

  BQPD = -lgalahad_bqpd

This allows GALAHAD to function, but any attempt
to use BQPD will result in an error return code.

If you wish to use BQPD, and you agree to the
licencing conditions (see the file LICENCE), you
may obtain a binary shared library for most common
systems. See 

  https://github.com/leyffer/BQPD_jll.jl/releases

N.B. The system you require may be hidden behind the
"Show all 50 assets" link, so please click this!
For modern Linux systems, the required binary files
are for x86_64-linux-gnu-libgfortran5, viz

  https://github.com/leyffer/BQPD_jll.jl/releases/download/BQPD-v1.0.0%2B0/BQPD.v1.0.0.x86_64-linux-gnu-libgfortran5.tar.gz

Make sure this is on your library search path, and set

  BQPD = -lbqpd -lbqpd_dense -lgalahad

